  "answer": "**No. Inflation is running above the RBA's 2–3% target band and has risen over the past year.**\n\n- **Headline CPI:** 4.0% year-on-year in August 2026, the latest monthly figure. It was 1.9% in June 2025 and peaked at 4.6% in March 2026.\n- **Trimmed mean (the RBA's preferred underlying measure):** 3.6% in August 2026, up from 2.8% in June 2025. It has been above 3% since July 2025 and has risen for several months.\n- **RBA response:** The cash rate was cut to 3.60% by late 2025, then raised from February 2026. The monthly average was 4.36% in September 2026, up from 3.60% in January.\n\nHeadline inflation has eased a little from its March peak, but the underlying trend is still rising, and the RBA is tightening policy in response. Inflation is therefore not yet under control. The September quarter CPI, due in late October, will be the next check.",
